window.EF_CRUX_DOC_PAGES=["INDUSTRIAL SECTOR — FULL MIND MAP\n                              Topic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n\n\nTopics in this chapter:\n 1. Major Companies, Regulators, CSR & Corporate Governance\n 2. Infrastructure, Corridors, Mobile Manufacturing, NIIF & PLI\n 3. National Manufacturing Policy, Make in India, Start-ups & Enterprise Finance\n 4. Industrial & Labour Laws, Industrial Growth, IIP & Core Sectors\n 5. MSME Definition, Classification, Investment Limits & Credit Guarantee\n 6. Small-Scale & Cottage Industries — Importance, Problems & Committees\n 7. Textiles, Paper, Fertilizers, Petroleum & Public Trading Enterprises\n 8. Public Sector Role, Major PSUs, Refineries, Energy & Services\n 9. Maharatna/Navratna/Miniratna, State Industrial Support & Business Concepts\n 10. Industrial Policy Resolutions, Licensing, Liberalisation & FMCG\n 11. Privatisation, Disinvestment & National Investment Fund\n 12. Steel, Aluminium, Cement, Industrial Centres & Organisation-Ministry Mapping\n 13. National Renewal Fund, Golden Handshake & Industrial Relations\n 14. Sugar, Cement, Textiles, Aluminium, Petrochemicals & Industrial Location\n 15. Industrial History, Business Groups, MNCs & Automobile Headquarters\n 16. Khadi, Textile Committees, RIICO, State Finance & Industrialists\n 17. e-Biz, E-Commerce, Information Technology & Software\n 18. Automobile, Pharmaceutical Sector & District Mineral Foundations\n\n\n 1. Major Companies, Regulators, CSR & Corporate Governance\n\n• Fortune Global 500 ke July 2006 edition mein Exxon Mobil top par tha aur Reliance Industries 284th rank par thi. 2024 Global 500\n mein Walmart overall first tha, jabki Indian companies mein Reliance Industries Ltd. overall rank 86 ke saath sabse upar thi. [Q1]\n• Fortune 500 India 2024 mein Reliance Industries ₹9,22,391 crore revenue ke saath largest company thi; LIC second, Indian Oil\n third aur ONGC fourth position par the. [Q2]\n• Reliance Industries US$200 billion market-cap cross karne wali first Indian company bani; yeh milestone September 2020 mein hi\n achieve ho gaya tha. [Q3]\n• Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board (PNGRB) 31 March 2006 ke Act ke under constitute hua, lekin yeh India ka first\n regulatory body nahi tha; KVIC, Forward Markets Commission, SEBI aur IRDA jaise bodies pehle se exist karte the. [Q4]\n• PCRA ka full form Petroleum Conservation Research Association hai. Petroleum Conservation Action Group (PCAG) 1976 mein\n petroleum products ki conservation aur efficient use ko promote karne ke liye set up hua tha. [Q5]\n• SDG India Index 2023-24 mein India ka national score 71 tha, jo 2020-21 ke 66 aur 2019-20 ke 60 se higher tha. Uttarakhand aur\n Kerala 79 score ke saath joint-best performing States rahe. [Q6]\n• Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) ka basic idea business ko social responsibilities fulfill karte hue conduct karna hai; CSR\n charity ya society par favour karna nahi hai. [Q7]\n• Business context mein social responsibility ka matlab self-regulation aur aise responsible actions hain jo society ki quality of life\n improve karein. Companies Act, 2013 ke CSR framework ke under specified net-worth/turnover/profit thresholds wali companies ko\n CSR Committee banani hoti hai aur prescribed profit share welfare activities par spend karna hota hai. [Q8]\n• India mein CSR framework Companies Act, 2013 ke Section 135, Schedule VII aur Companies (CSR Policy) Rules, 2014 se govern\n hota hai; ye CSR eligibility, implementation aur reporting ke rules define karte hain. [Q9]\n• SEBI ne June 2017 mein Kotak Committee ko listed entities ke corporate-governance reforms suggest karne ke liye constitute kiya;\n committee ne October 2017 mein report submit ki. Committee ne Chairman aur Managing Director roles ke governance structure par\n recommendations di thi. [Q10]\n\n EXAM TRAP — Corporate / SDG Data Changes by Year\n ▸ Fortune rankings, market-cap milestones aur SDG Index scores year-specific hote hain; later update historical figure ko\n automatically replace nahi karta.\n [Q1, Q2, Q3, Q6]\n\n\n\n\n 2. Infrastructure, Corridors, Mobile Manufacturing, NIIF & PLI\n\n• Indian Railways ne 2030 tak net-zero carbon-emission network aur 2023 tak 100% electrification ka target set kiya tha. [Q11]\n• India ka first rubber-tyre based metro project Nashik, Maharashtra mein develop kiya gaya. [Q12]\n• Swedish retailer IKEA ne India ka first showroom 9 August 2018 ko Hyderabad mein open kiya; company ne India mein multiple\n stores expand karne ka plan banaya tha. [Q13]\n• Industrial Development Centre Banmore, Madhya Pradesh ke Morena district mein located hai. [Q14]\n• Madhya Pradesh ke Dewas ko pharmaceutical products aur Indore ko soya meal/soya products ke liye Towns of Export Excellence\n mein include kiya gaya. [Q15]\n• Budget 2015-16 ke baad infrastructure PPP model ko revisit aur revitalize karne ke liye Dr. Vijay Kelkar ke chairmanship mein\n committee constitute ki gayi. [Q16]","• Bharatmala Pariyojana highways-sector ki umbrella scheme hai; economic corridors, border/international-connectivity roads,\ncoastal-port roads aur expressways jaise road infrastructure ko develop/improve karna iska focus hai. [Q17]\n• National Infrastructure Pipeline Task Force ki final report 29 April 2020 ko release hui. NIP ka objective world-class infrastructure\ndevelop karke citizens ki quality of life improve karna hai. [Q18]\n• PM Gati Shakti National Master Plan 13 October 2021 ko launch hua. Is framework mein roads, railways, airports, ports, mass\ntransport, waterways aur logistics infrastructure—seven engines—ko integrated planning se align kiya jaata hai. [Q19]\n• Delhi-Mumbai Industrial/Economic Corridor Japan ke collaboration se develop kiya ja raha hai; India-Japan agreement 2006 mein\nsign hua tha. [Q20]\n• 2019-23 infrastructure expenditure ke compared States mein Uttar Pradesh first, Maharashtra second, Tamil Nadu third aur\nKarnataka fourth tha. [Q21]\n• Deepak Parekh Committee May 2007 mein infrastructure development aur financing ke measures suggest karne ke liye constitute\nki gayi thi. [Q22]\n• Mobile-gaming market ko downloads ke basis par dekhen to India top par hai; revenue basis par India top-5 countries mein nahi\naata. [Q23]\n• Indian Cellular Association ke April 2018 data mein India 2017 tak mobile-phone manufacturing mein China ke baad second\nposition par pahunch gaya tha; February 2025 tak ke data mein bhi India second-largest mobile-phone manufacturing country raha.\n[Q24]\n• 2023 mein mobile-phone manufacturing mein India ka global position second tha. [Q25]\n• National Investment and Infrastructure Fund (NIIF) Indian Trusts Act, 1882 ke framework mein investment trust ke roop mein\nregistered hai; yeh NITI Aayog ka organ nahi hai. Proposed corpus ₹40,000 crore tha. [Q26]\n• Production Linked Incentive (PLI) scheme 2021 mein 14 important sectors ke liye announce hui, taaki India ki manufacturing\ncapacity aur exports ko boost kiya ja sake. [Q27]\n\nEXAM TRAP — Infrastructure Timelines\n▸ NIP, PM Gati Shakti, mobile manufacturing aur PLI ke launch year/period aur target details alag hain; in timelines ko interchange na\nkarein.\n[Q18, Q19, Q24, Q25, Q27]\n\n\n\n\n3. National Manufacturing Policy, Make in India, Start-ups & Enterprise Finance\n\n• National Manufacturing Policy (NMP) ko Ministry of Commerce and Industry ne 4 November 2011 ko notify kiya. [Q28]\n• National Manufacturing Policy 2011 mein launch/notified hui. [Q29]\n• National Manufacturing Policy ka target manufacturing growth 12-14%, better global competitiveness aur faster exports tha; 100\nmillion jobs ka target 2022 ke liye tha, 2025 ke liye nahi. [Q30]\n• Manufacturing-sector growth support karne ke liye National Investment and Manufacturing Zones (NIMZs), Single Window\nClearance aur Technology Acquisition and Development Fund jaise mechanisms provide kiye gaye. [Q31]\n• National Investment and Manufacturing Zones (NIMZs) NMP 2011 ke key instruments hain—large integrated industrial townships\njahan modern infrastructure, clean technology, social infrastructure aur skill facilities hoti hain. DMIC-linked examples mein\nAhmedabad-Dholera, Shendra-Bidkin, Manesar-Bawal, Khushkhera-Bhiwadi-Neemrana, Pithampur-Dhar-Mhow, Dadri-Noida-\nGhaziabad, Dighi Port aur Jodhpur-Pali-Marwar shamil hain. [Q32]\n• Capital intensity production process mein labour ke comparison mein machinery/equipment jaise capital ka relative use batata hai.\nHigh capital intensity mein capital ka use zyada hota hai; 2017-18 ke compared States mein manufacturing capital intensity Madhya\nPradesh mein highest thi. [Q33]\n• Make in India 25 September 2014 ko launch hua aur iska logo Lion hai. Iske objectives bureaucracy/red-tapism reduce karna,\ninfrastructure improve karke manufacturing cost kam karna, competitiveness badhana aur Ease of Doing Business improve karna\nthe. [Q34]\n• 'Make in India' program September, 2014 mein launch hua. [Q35]\n• 'Make in India' program ka logo Lion hai. [Q36]\n• Make in India ka objective investment facilitate karna, India ko major investment destination banana aur companies ko India mein\nmanufacture karne ke liye encourage karke global manufacturing hub develop karna hai. [Q37]\n• Digital India Government ka flagship programme hai jiska vision digitally empowered society aur knowledge economy banana hai.\nIska focus government departments ko citizens se digitally connect karke services ko paperless/electronic mode mein accessible\nbanana hai. [Q38]\n• Start-ups ki financing needs ko Angel Investors, Venture Capital aur Crowd Funding jaise new-generation funding sources support\nkarte hain. [Q39]\n• Start-up generally naya enterprise hota hai jo innovative product/service market mein introduce karta hai. Start-up financing ke liye\nsingle funding source ke bajay hybrid funding model ka approach important maana gaya hai. [Q40]\n• Gujarat Government ne January 2022 mein Student Start-up and Innovation Policy (SSIP) 2.0 launch ki; policy period 11 January\n2022 se 31 March 2027 tak tha. [Q41]\n• Stand Up India entrepreneurship aur employment promote karne ke liye announce hui; scheme 5 April 2016 ko Noida se launch ki\ngayi aur SC/ST aur women entrepreneurs ko institutional credit access dene par focus karti hai. [Q42]","• Stand-up India SC/ST aur women entrepreneurs ko institutional credit structure tak access facilitate karta hai. Scheme 5 April 2016\nko Noida, Uttar Pradesh se launch hui, Babu Jagjivan Ram ki birth anniversary aur Dr. Bhimrao Ambedkar ki 125th birth anniversary\nke occasion par. [Q43]\n• Stand-Up India entrepreneurship scheme women, SCs aur STs ko promote karti hai. [Q44]\n• Pradhan Mantri MUDRA Yojana (PMMY) Department of Financial Services, Ministry of Finance ke under operate hoti hai aur 8 April\n2015 ko launch hui. [Q45]\n• PM MUDRA Yojana ka aim micro entrepreneurs ko formal financial system se jodna aur 'Funding the Unfunded' ke through credit\nsupport dena hai. MUDRA ka full form Micro Units Development and Refinance Agency hai. [Q46]\n• PM MUDRA Yojana small non-farm income-generating businesses ko easy credit support deti hai. Original framework mein ₹10\nlakh tak ke loans Shishu/Kishor/Tarun categories ke through cover hote the. [Q47]\n• MUDRA ki Kishor category mein loan amount ₹50,000 se zyada aur ₹5 lakh tak hota hai. [Q48]\n• PMMY ne non-corporate, non-farm micro/small enterprises ko collateral-light credit access diya. Union Budget 2024-25 mein\neligible successful borrowers ke liye loan limit ₹20 lakh tak badhane ki announcement hui. [Q49]\n• Mukhyamantri Udyam Kranti Yojana Madhya Pradesh mein self-employment ke liye collateral-free/easy loan support dene ke\nobjective se April 2022 mein launch hui. [Q50]\n• Quality Council of India (QCI) 1996 ke Cabinet decision se national quality body ke roop mein establish hua; iske formation mein\nEU expert mission aur inter-ministerial consultation ka role tha. [Q51]\n\n\n4. Industrial & Labour Laws, Industrial Growth, IIP & Core Sectors\n\n• Important industrial-law chronology: Minimum Wages Act—1948; Industries (Development and Regulation) Act—1951; MRTP Act—\n1969; FERA—1973. [Q52]\n• Monopolies and Restrictive Trade Practices Commission (MRTPC), MRTP Act 1969 ke Section 5 ke under establish hua. [Q53]\n• Labour Bureau labour-related statistics ki collection, analysis aur dissemination karta hai aur Ministry of Labour & Employment ka\nattached office hai; iski institutional roots 1920 se hain. [Q54]\n• Trade Disputes Act, 1929 ne trade disputes ke investigation/settlement ke liye Board of Conciliation aur Court of Inquiry ka\nframework diya; strikes par restrictions bhi is framework ka part the. [Q55]\n• Industrial Employment (Standing Orders) Central Amendment Rules, 2018 ne fixed-term employment ko apparel manufacturing se\nextend karke all sectors tak applicable kiya. [Q56]\n• India ka first Factories Act 1881 mein pass hua. Ismein mainly child workers ki safety se related provisions the; women workers ke\nliye specific provisions nahi the. [Q57]\n• Code on Wages, 2019 wages aur bonus se related multiple labour laws ko consolidate aur amend karne ke liye banaya gaya\nframework hai. [Q58]\n• Casual worker temporary employment arrangement par kaam karta hai, jisme job security aur benefits limited ho sakte hain. EPF\ncoverage mein company se directly/indirectly wages draw karne wale eligible employees provident-fund benefits claim kar sakte\nhain. [Q59]\n• Uttar Pradesh mein 1 April 2017 se unskilled worker ka minimum wage ₹7,400/month tha. 1 October 2025 se 31 March 2026 period\nke rates: Unskilled ₹11,021; Semi-skilled ₹12,123; Skilled ₹13,580 per month. [Q60]\n• 2006-07 ke historical data mein industry ka India ke GDP mein share roughly 25-30% range mein tha; exact share series aur price-\nbase ke saath change hota hai. [Q61]\n• Economic Review 2025-26 mein industrial-sector growth FY2024-25 ke liye 5.9% aur FY2025-26 ke first half ke liye around 7%\nrecord ki gayi. [Q62]\n• 1999-2000 mein industrial-production growth 6.7% thi, jo 1998-99 ke 4.1% se higher thi. South-East Asian currency crisis aur\nnuclear-test sanctions ke backdrop ke bawajood 1999-2000 period mein exchange rate relative stability dikhata hai. [Q63]\n• Recent IIP use-based data mein capital goods aur infrastructure/construction goods ne strong growth record ki. [Q64]\n• Index of Industrial Production (IIP) NSO calculate/release karta hai. Broad-sector IIP mein mining, manufacturing aur electricity;\nuse-based IIP mein primary, capital, intermediate, infrastructure/construction, consumer durables aur consumer non-durables shamil\nhote hain. [Q65]\n• IIP ke broad-sector coverage mein mining, manufacturing aur electricity shamil hain; gas aur water supply is group ka part nahi\nhain. [Q66]\n• Index of Industrial Production (IIP) India mein National Statistical Office (NSO) ki Economic Statistics Division release karti hai.\n[Q67]\n• IIP series ka base year June 2011 release mein 1993-94 se 2004-05 shift hua; May 2017 ki new series mein base 2011-12 hua. Is\nseries mein mining 14.37%, manufacturing 77.63% aur electricity 7.99% weight carry karte hain; 839 items aur 407 item-groups\ncover hue. [Q68]\n• India ke eight core industries hain: Coal, Crude Oil, Natural Gas, Petroleum Refinery Products, Fertilizers, Steel, Cement aur\nElectricity. [Q69]\n• Chemicals eight core industries ka part nahi hai. [Q70]\n• Eight Core Industries ka combined index Coal, Crude Oil, Natural Gas, Petroleum Refinery Products, Fertilizers, Steel, Cement aur\nElectricity ko cover karta hai. Current IIP-linked weights mein Petroleum Refinery Products 28.04% ke saath highest aur Electricity\n19.85% hai. [Q71]\n• 2000-01 mein listed industries mein steel ki growth rate sabse zyada thi. 20 January 2026 ko released core-industry data mein\n2024-25 se 2025-26 (April-December, provisional) ke beech overall growth 4.5% se 2.6% hui; steel 6.8% se 9.5% aur cement 6.3%\nse 8.8% raha. [Q72]","• Coal-block allocation currently auction se hota hai, lottery se nahi. Domestic coal-supply shortage ko meet karne ke liye imports bhi\nkiye jaate hain. [Q73]\n• Manufacturing ka matlab machines, tools aur labour ke through raw materials ko large scale par finished goods mein convert karna\nhai. Construction industry ko manufacturing se separate category maana jaata hai. [Q74]\n\nEXAM TRAP — IIP vs Eight Core Industries\n▸ IIP aur Eight Core Industries alag measures hain; inke base years, weights aur series structure ko mix nahi karna\nchahiye.\n[Q62, Q64, Q65, Q66, Q67, Q68, Q69, Q70, Q71]\n\n\n\n\n5. MSME Definition, Classification, Investment Limits & Credit Guarantee\n\n• MSMED Act 2006 ke 14 saal baad Atmanirbhar Bharat Package mein 13 May 2020 ko MSME definition revise karne ki\nannouncement hui; manufacturing aur service units ke liye uniform investment-turnover formula adopt hua. [Q75]\n• Investment aur turnover based revised MSME classification 2020 mein introduce hui. [Q76]\n• 1991 Industrial Policy mein small-unit investment limit ₹35 lakh se ₹60 lakh aur ancillary-industry limit ₹45 lakh se ₹75 lakh ki gayi.\n[Q77]\n• 2020 revision mein micro enterprise ke liye plant/machinery/equipment investment limit ₹1 crore tak rakhi gayi; yeh MSME definition\nreform Atmanirbhar Bharat Package ka part tha. [Q78]\n• 2020 MSME classification mein micro enterprise ke liye investment limit ₹1 crore aur turnover limit ₹5 crore thi. 1 April 2025 se\nrevised classification mein micro enterprise ki limits investment up to ₹2.5 crore aur annual turnover up to ₹10 crore hain. [Q79]\n• Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development (MSMED) Act 2006 mein enacted hua. [Q80]\n• New Industrial Policy 1991 ke period mein small-scale industries ki capital-investment limit ₹60 lakh thi. [Q81]\n• Old MSME manufacturing classification mein small enterprise ka plant/machinery investment ₹25 lakh se zyada aur ₹5 crore tak\ntha. [Q82]\n• MSMED Act, 2006 ke original classification mein medium enterprise ka investment band ₹5 crore se ₹10 crore tha. [Q83]\n• MSMED Act, 2006 ke original manufacturing-sector classification mein medium enterprise ke liye investment ₹5 crore se zyada aur\n₹10 crore se kam tha. [Q84]\n• MSMED Act, 2006 ne micro, small aur medium enterprises ko manufacturing aur service—do broad categories mein classify karke\nseparate investment limits define ki thi. [Q85]\n• MSMED Act, 2006 ke original framework mein manufacturing enterprises ko plant aur machinery investment ke basis par micro,\nsmall aur medium categories mein classify kiya gaya tha. [Q86]\n• CGTMSE ka full form Credit Guarantee Fund Trust for Micro and Small Enterprises hai. Government of India aur SIDBI ne 2000\nmein ise collateral-free credit support ke liye jointly launch kiya. [Q87]\n\n\n6. Small-Scale & Cottage Industries — Importance, Problems & Committees\n\n• ASI 2022-23 ke hisaab se total factories mein top States ka order tha: Tamil Nadu (39,666) > Gujarat (31,031) > Maharashtra\n(26,446) > Uttar Pradesh (19,102) > Andhra Pradesh (16,483). [Q88]\n• Large-scale industries generally capital aur technology intensive hoti hain, jabki small-scale industries labour intensive hoti hain.\nIsliye per unit capital investment par small-scale sector relatively zyada employment generate karta hai. [Q89]\n• Small-scale aur cottage industries ki khas importance employment generation hai. Ye labour-intensive hoti hain, isliye labour-\nsurplus developing economy jaise India mein per unit capital zyada jobs create karti hain. [Q90]\n• Small-scale/cottage industries ka major importance employment generation hai. Third SSI Census context mein employment 1998-\n99 ke 220.55 lakh se badhkar Fourth All India Census 2009-10 mein around 659 lakh report hua. [Q91]\n• Handloom India ke sabse important small-scale industries mein se ek hai aur diverse cultural heritage ko represent karta hai.\nMuslin, chintz, rugs aur khadi jaise products is sector se jude hain; handloom largely unorganised sector ka part hai. [Q92]\n• Current data mein these industries ke beech Uttar Pradesh mein employment ke terms mein handloom industry sabse badi hai.\n[Q93]\n• Indian small-scale industries ki major problems hain: capital ki kami, marketing difficulty, raw-material shortage, infrastructure\nconstraints, delayed payments, industrial sickness aur reliable quality data ki kami. [Q94]\n• Small aur cottage industries ko raw material, finance, outdated production methods, marketing aur large industries se competition\njaise challenges face hote hain. Organisation, research, transport aur technical education ki kami bhi important problems hain;\nstrikes-lockouts mainly large industries se associated issue hai. [Q95]\n• Small-enterprise committees ki chronology: Karve Committee (1955) → Nayak Committee (1991) → Abid Hussain Committee\n(1995) → S. S. Kohli Committee (2000). [Q96]\n• Nayak Committee December 1991 mein RBI ne small-scale industry sector ki finance aur sickness-related problems evaluate karne\nke liye constitute ki; committee ne September 1992 mein report submit ki. [Q97]\n• Small Enterprises par Expert Committee December 1995 mein Dr. Abid Hussain ki chairmanship mein constitute hui thi, jiska\npurpose small enterprises ki problems study karke development suggestions dena tha. [Q98]\n• Abid Hussain Committee Small and Medium Enterprises se related thi. [Q99]","• 1992 ke aas-paas small-scale industry ka manufacturing turnover contribution around 40% category mein tha. Economic Survey\n2025-26 mein MSMEs ka manufacturing contribution around 35.4%, exports 48.58% aur GDP 31.3% diya gaya; sector large-scale\nemployment bhi generate karta hai. [Q100]\n• MSME sector ka GVA-to-GDP ratio 2020-21 mein 27.3% aur 2022-23 mein 30.1% tha. Ye MSME GVA ka GDP mein share hai,\ncountry ke total GVA mein share wali wording se ise confuse na karein. [Q101]\n• Cooperative units mein cotton textile industry ne strong growth dikhayi; 1999-2000 se 2005-06 ke period mein year-on-year growth\nlagbhag 14.8% record hui. [Q102]\n\nEXAM TRAP — Committee Chronology\n▸ Committee chronology: Karve 1955 → Nayak 1991 → Abid Hussain 1995 → S. S. Kohli 2000.\n[Q96]\n\n\n\n\n7. Textiles, Paper, Fertilizers, Petroleum & Public Trading Enterprises\n\n• Textile industry agriculture ke baad India ke sabse bade employment generators mein se ek hai. Manufacturing GVA mein iska\ncontribution around 11% raha; Economic Survey/Review 2025-26 context mein apparel-textile industry ka size roughly US$179\nbillion aur GDP contribution around 2% bataya gaya. [Q103]\n• India mein textiles industry major employment-generating industries mein se ek hai. [Q104]\n• India mein cotton textiles ka largest share powerloom sector produce karta hai—historical composition mein 60% se zyada. Uske\nbaad hosiery, handloom aur mill sectors ka contribution aata hai. [Q105]\n• Mumbai ko 'Cotton Polis of India' kaha jaata hai; Ahmedabad bhi India ka major cotton-textile centre hai. [Q106]\n• October 2020 mein Tamil Nadu mein cotton mills ki sankhya sabse zyada thi, uske baad Maharashtra; listed States mein\nMaharashtra sabse upar tha. [Q107]\n• Historical cloth-production composition mein mill-made 4%, handloom 12%, hosiery 22% aur powerloom 62% share tha. Listed\nStates ke mill-made cloth data mein Gujarat sabse aage tha. [Q108]\n• Textile industry India ki oldest large industries mein se hai. First modern cotton-mill attempt 1818 mein Calcutta (Kolkata) ke paas\nhua tha. [Q109]\n• India mein cottage industries ka development bahut purana hai. Colonial period se pehle industrial production mein inka major\ncontribution tha aur fine cotton textiles bhi cottage level par produce hote the. [Q110]\n• Iron and steel ko modern industry ki core/pivotal industry maana jaata hai, jabki petrochemical sector ko growth industry ke roop\nmein dekha jaata hai. [Q111]\n• NEPA Limited, Nepanagar (Madhya Pradesh) newsprint production ka important centre raha hai. [Q112]\n• Yamunanagar (Haryana), Guwahati (Assam) aur Ballarpur (Maharashtra) paper-industry centres hain; Shahabad (Bihar) ko is group\nmein paper-manufacturing centre nahi maana jaata. [Q113]\n• Government ne 1972 mein Korba, Chhattisgarh mein coal-based fertilizer plant establish karne ko approve kiya tha. [Q114]\n• KRIBHCO ka Hazira fertilizer plant, Surat ke paas Hazira mein located hai aur natural gas based plant hai. [Q115]\n• India ne chemical-fertilizer production mein substantial self-sufficiency develop ki hai. [Q116]\n• Fertilizer production mein natural gas important feedstock hai; isi wajah se domestic natural-gas resources fertilizer industry ke liye\nstrategically important hain. [Q117]\n• ONGC ki institutional beginning 14 August 1956 ko Oil and Natural Gas Commission ke roop mein hui; October 1959 mein statutory\nstatus mila. Headquarters Dehradun, Uttarakhand mein hai. [Q118]\n• Oil India Limited (OIL) public-sector enterprise hai jo crude oil aur natural gas ki exploration, development, production aur oil\ntransportation se linked hai; ise Maharatna status mil chuka hai. [Q119]\n• MMTC India ka major non-oil importer hai aur Projects & Equipment Corporation Ministry of Commerce and Industry ke under hai.\nExport Credit Guarantee Corporation ka role export-credit risk cover hai; export goods ki quality-control/pre-shipment inspection iska\nobjective nahi hai. [Q120]\n• MMTC Limited Government of India undertaking aur major international trading organisation hai. Neelachal Ispat Nigam Limited\n(NINL) Odisha ke Jajpur district mein located hai. [Q121]\n• MMTC public sector ka major trading organisation aur minerals exporter raha hai; foreign-exchange earnings mein bhi iska\nimportant role raha. [Q122]\n\n\n8. Public Sector Role, Major PSUs, Refineries, Energy & Services\n\n• Public sector ke objectives mein public utilities provide karna, social-economic infrastructure build karna, balanced regional/sectoral\ndevelopment promote karna aur income-wealth redistribution ke through egalitarian goals support karna shamil hain. [Q123]\n• Self-reliance ke liye public investment power, steel, aluminium, copper, mining, heavy machinery aur paper jaise basic industries\nmein kiya gaya. Public-sector jobs mein security relatively high ho sakti hai, lekin har PSU profitable ho—ye zaroori nahi. [Q124]\n• 1991 ke baad New Economic Policy ka major emphasis private-sector role badhane par raha; public-sector employment growth\ninitially very low aur later negative bhi raha. [Q125]\n• Public sector ka role kai major areas mein raha hai, lekin commercial banking functions mein iska presence sabse effective raha.\n[Q126]","• TISCO, ab Tata Steel, private-sector steel company hai; 1907 mein Jamshedpur mein establish hui. NTPC, SAIL aur BHEL public-\nsector Maharatna companies hain. [Q127]\n• Ordnance Factory Jabalpur, BHEL Bhopal aur Opium & Alkaloid Factory Neemuch Central Government establishments hain;\nGwalior ki leather factory private-sector unit thi. [Q128]\n• ESSAR Oil, ab Nayara Energy Limited, private-sector enterprise hai; comparison ke other enterprises public-sector category mein\naate hain. [Q129]\n• BHEL ka Bhopal unit August 1956 mein Heavy Electrical Plant (HEP) Limited ke roop mein establish hua tha. Heavy electrical\nmachinery/equipment ke production ke liye British Associated Electrical Industries ke collaboration ka role tha. [Q130]\n• BPCL mein Government of India ki stake pehle 66.2% thi; March 2020 ke end se reported government stake 52.98% rahi. [Q131]\n• Balmer Lawrie & Company aur Educational Consultants India Ltd. public-sector enterprises hain. Dredging Corporation of India bhi\npublic-sector company thi, lekin 2017 mein private-sector company mein transform hui. [Q132]\n• Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board (PNGRB) PNGRB Act, 2006 ke under establish hua. Board ka regulation refining,\nstorage, transportation, distribution, marketing aur sale par apply hota hai; petroleum/natural-gas production iske regulatory scope ka\npart nahi hai. [Q133]\n• Current ownership structure mein Essar Oil/Nayara Energy private sector mein hai. Bongaigaon aur Haldia refineries IOC ke under\nhain, jabki Mangalore Refinery (MRPL) ONGC subsidiary hai. [Q134]\n• Is comparison mein listed oil refineries public-sector refineries hain; inmein private-sector refinery include nahi hai. [Q135]\n• India mein Koyali historically high-capacity public refinery centres mein raha, jabki Reliance ka Jamnagar refinery complex country\nka highest-capacity refinery complex aur world ke largest refinery complexes mein se ek hai. [Q136]\n• Jamnagar, Gujarat petrochemical industry ka major centre hai; Dahej bhi important petrochemical hub hai. Jamnagar refinery\ncomplex global-scale capacity ke liye known hai. [Q137]\n• Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL) aircraft aur aerospace equipment se associated PSU hai; October 2024 mein HAL ko\nMaharatna status mila. [Q138]\n• NHPC Limited power-generation company hai, primarily hydroelectric sector se linked. 1975 mein establish hui aur solar/wind\nprojects mein bhi activity rakhti hai. [Q139]\n• India Tourism Development Corporation (ITDC) tourism aur hotel infrastructure/development se associated public-sector\norganisation hai. [Q140]\n• Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL) year 2000 mein establish hua. [Q141]\n• BSNL mein Government of India ka 100% ownership raha, jabki NTPC, BHEL aur SBI jaise listed public-sector entities mein\ngovernment stake 100% se kam hai. [Q142]\n• BSNL loss-making CPSE raha. BSNL Annual Report 2023-24 mein 2023-24 ka loss ₹5,370.73 crore tha, jabki 2022-23 mein\n₹8,161.56 crore loss report hua. [Q143]\n• 2014-15 mein Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited loss-making CPSEs mein shamil tha. [Q144]\n• GAIL ne Vijayawada (Andhra Pradesh) se Vijaipur (Madhya Pradesh) pipeline project ke liye around ₹8,000 crore ka\nprovision/planned investment rakha tha. [Q145]\n• Petrol aur diesel pricing India mein deregulated framework par operate karti hai; retail prices oil-marketing companies market-linked\nfactors ke basis par determine karti hain. [Q146]\n\nEXAM TRAP — Private Refinery Data Mismatch\n▸ Refinery ownership: Bongaigaon aur Haldia IOC/public-sector network mein hain; Nayara Energy (erstwhile Essar Oil)\nprivate sector mein hai; MRPL ONGC subsidiary hai.\n[Q135]\n\n\n\n\n9. Maharatna/Navratna/Miniratna, State Industrial Support & Business Concepts\n\n• Navratna status select Central Public Sector Enterprises ko greater managerial/financial autonomy dene ke liye diya jaata hai,\nespecially un enterprises ko jinke global-scale growth potential ko recognise kiya gaya ho. [Q147]\n• Oil India Limited ko August 2023 mein 13th Maharatna CPSE ka status mila; December 2025 tak bhi company Maharatna category\nmein thi. [Q148]\n• January 2020 ki Maharatna list mein Oil India Limited Maharatna category mein included nahi tha. [Q149]\n• Maharatna scheme ke early phase mein November 2010 mein IOC, NTPC, ONGC aur SAIL ko Maharatna status diya gaya tha.\n[Q150]\n• Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL) Navratna company hai; comparison mein diye gaye kai other large CPSEs Maharatna category\nmein aate hain. [Q151]\n• BHEL aur GAIL ko 2013 mein Maharatna status grant kiya gaya. [Q152]\n• Maharatna companies ki count time ke saath badli—older period mein 10 ka figure milta hai, jabki December 2025 tak count 14 tha.\n[Q153]\n• Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL) Navratna category mein hai; Coal India, BHEL aur GAIL Maharatna category mein hain. [Q154]\n• MTNL Navratna category se associated raha hai, jabki GAIL aur SAIL Maharatna companies hain. [Q155]\n• Older PSU-status comparisons mein Indian Aluminium ko exception ke roop mein diya gaya tha; current classification mein SAIL,\nPower Grid aur REC jaise enterprises Maharatna category mein hain. [Q156]","• National Aluminium Company Limited (NALCO) 1981 mein incorporated hui aur Navratna CPSE hai. [Q157]\n• Miniratna Category-I status ke liye CPSE ko prescribed profitability/net-worth conditions fulfil karni hoti hain. Is status ke saath\nBoard ko certain investment decisions mein greater autonomy milti hai; traditional limit ₹500 crore tak ke projects ke context mein\npoochhi gayi hai. [Q158]\n• September 2006 mein BSNL, BEML, Hindustan Latex, EPIL, RINL aur GRSE ko additional Miniratna status mila; Indian Telephone\nIndustries us six-unit list mein nahi thi. December 2025 tak RINL Navratna status mein tha. [Q159]\n• Policy-year mapping: Information Technology Policy—2000; Hotel Policy—2006; Industrial and Investment Promotion Policy—2010;\nMineral Policy—2011. [Q160]\n• Udyami Helpline August 2010 mein entrepreneurs ko information aur guidance support dene ke liye launch ki gayi. [Q161]\n• Madhya Pradesh Financial Corporation SMEs ko state-level financial assistance provide karta hai. Headquarters Indore mein hai\naur institution ki roots 1955 ke Madhya Bharat Financial Corporation se judi hain. [Q162]\n• Uttar Pradesh mein small aur medium enterprises ko long-term loans U.P. Small Industries Corporation, U.P. Industrial\nDevelopment Corporation aur U.P. Financial Corporation jaise institutions provide karte hain. [Q163]\n• Uttar Pradesh Financial Corporation 1954 mein industrial development ke liye establish hua; tourism-related industry ko chhodkar\neligible industrial activities ko finance support deta tha. [Q164]\n• Udyog Bandhu Uttar Pradesh mein industrial units/investors ko facilitation aur problem-resolution support provide karne wali\ninitiative/institutional mechanism hai. [Q165]\n• Uttar Pradesh mein industrial development ke context mein western region comparatively sabse developed maana jaata hai. [Q166]\n• Board for Industrial and Financial Reconstruction (BIFR) sick industrial companies ke revival/rehabilitation framework se associated\nbody thi; iska operational phase 1987 se start hua. [Q167]\n• Mega Food Park Scheme September 2008 mein food-processing industry ke infrastructure ko improve karne ke objective se\napprove hui. [Q168]\n• Mega Food Parks ka focus food-processing industry ke liye modern infrastructure dena aur perishables ki processing badha kar\nwastage reduce karna hai. [Q169]\n• Foreign trade aur industrial development GDP growth ko exports, imports of technology/capital goods, market expansion aur\nproductivity channels ke through support karte hain. [Q170]\n• Business enterprise ka objective sirf profit nahi hota; economic efficiency ke saath employment, consumer service aur broader\nsocial objectives bhi important ho sakte hain. [Q171]\n• Global liberalisation ke environment mein firms ko competitiveness maintain karne ke liye process re-engineering, technology\nupgradation aur productivity improvement par focus karna padta hai. [Q172]\n• Sole proprietorship mein proprietor ki liability unlimited hoti hai, jabki partnership contractual relationship par based business form\nhai. [Q173]\n• Capital expenditure (CapEx) physical assets ki acquisition, upgradation aur major maintenance par kiya gaya long-term expenditure\nhai; technology/equipment acquisition bhi capital investment ka part ho sakta hai. [Q174]\n• Venture capital new/high-growth enterprises ko long-term risk capital provide karta hai aur business expansion/innovation ko\nfinance karne ka important source hai. [Q175]\n\nEXAM TRAP — Maharatna / Navratna Status Changes Over Time\n▸ Maharatna/Navratna company status aur total count time ke saath change hote hain; dated list aur current list alag ho\nsakti hain.\n[Q147, Q148, Q149, Q150, Q151, Q152, Q153, Q154, Q155, Q156, Q157, Q158, Q159]\n\n\n\n\n10. Industrial Policy Resolutions, Licensing, Liberalisation & FMCG\n\n• Independent India ki first Industrial Policy 6 April 1948 ko Industry Minister Dr. Syama Prasad Mookerjee ne announce ki; isne\nmixed aur controlled economy ke industrial framework ki foundation rakhi. [Q176]\n• Industrial Policy Resolution 1956 independent India ki second major industrial policy resolution thi aur rapid industrialisation, public-\nsector role aur mixed-economy framework ko strengthen karti thi. [Q177]\n• Industrial Policy Resolution 1956 heavy industries mein State role ko strengthen karne aur Second Five Year Plan framework ko\nsupport karne ke context mein adopt hua; industries ko three schedules/categories mein classify kiya gaya. [Q178]\n• Industrial licensing ka statutory base Industries (Development and Regulation) Act, 1951 tha. New Industrial Policy, 1991 ke baad\nlicensing substantially liberalize hui; current framework mein compulsory licensing sirf a few specified industry groups tak limited hai.\n[Q179]\n• 1991 economic reforms mein sabse major structural changes Industrial Policy ke through aaye, kyunki liberalisation, privatisation\naur globalisation ke principles licensing, public sector, foreign investment aur technology policy se directly linked the. [Q180]\n• ISO 9001/9002 quality-management standards se linked hain. 1991 Industrial Policy ne industrial licensing ko substantially\nliberalise kiya. [Q181]\n• 1991 Industrial Policy ke time compulsory licensing 18 industries tak limited ki gayi thi; April 1993 mein ye list further reduce hokar\n15 industries reh gayi. [Q182]\n• Earlier licensing regime mein 15 industries licensing ke under thi; current DPIIT framework mein compulsory licensing four specified\nindustry groups tak limited hai. [Q183]","• India mein Liberalisation-Privatisation-Globalisation (LPG) based New Economic Policy 1991 mein P. V. Narasimha Rao\nGovernment ke period mein announce hui. [Q184]\n• 1991 Industrial Policy par major criticisms mein agriculture ko insufficient attention, implementation ambiguity aur social/regional\nconcerns shamil rahe. [Q185]\n• White goods generally durable consumer appliances ko refer karte hain—jaise refrigerator, washing machine, air-conditioner etc.;\nconspicuous consumption context mein bhi ye category poochhi ja sakti hai. [Q186]\n• Indian Petrochemicals Corporation Ltd. (IPCL) ka Reliance Industries Group mein merger ho chuka hai, aur MTNL ab NYSE par\nlisted nahi hai. December 2025 data mein Reliance Industries Ltd. market capitalization aur revenue ke basis par India ki largest\nprivate company thi. [Q187]\n• FMCG (Fast-Moving Consumer Goods) high-turnover, relatively low-unit-value non-durable packaged goods hote hain. Cosmetics,\ndairy aur bakery products examples hain; vehicles durable goods hain, FMCG nahi. [Q188]\n\n\n11. Privatisation, Disinvestment & National Investment Fund\n\n• Full privatisation mein enterprise ka ownership aur management control public sector se private sector ko transfer ho jaata hai.\n[Q189]\n• Disinvestment ke objectives mein government ka financial burden reduce karna, public finances improve karna, market\ndiscipline/competition badhana aur enterprise efficiency enhance karna shamil hain. [Q190]\n• National Investment Fund (NIF) November 2005 mein establish hua; profitable CPSEs mein Central Government ki minority\nshareholding ke disinvestment proceeds ko is fund framework se link kiya gaya, jo Consolidated Fund se separate structure mein\nmaintained tha. [Q191]\n• Liberalisation ka core idea unnecessary controls aur restrictions ko reduce karna hai; disinvestment wider economic-reform\nframework ka important component raha. [Q192]\n• 1991 reforms ke baad public-sector reserved role reduce hua aur government ne CPSEs mein disinvestment programme\nstart/expand kiya. [Q193]\n• Public-sector disinvestment India mein 1991-92 financial year se start hua. [Q194]\nEXAM TRAP — Disinvestment: Policy Logic vs Historical Year\n▸ Disinvestment objectives, National Investment Fund aur programme start-year alag facts hain; policy role aur dates ek-\ndoosre se distinct hain.\n[Q189, Q190, Q191, Q192, Q193, Q194]\n\n\n\n\n12. Steel, Aluminium, Cement, Industrial Centres & Organisation-Ministry Mapping\n\n• Major steel-plant collaborations: Bhilai—USSR; Rourkela—West Germany; Durgapur—United Kingdom; Bokaro—USSR. Ye\nmapping Indian public-sector steel development ke liye important hai. [Q195]\n• Bhilai Steel Plant Soviet Union/Russia ke collaboration se establish hua. [Q196]\n• Bhilai Steel Plant public-sector enterprise hai. [Q197]\n• Rourkela Steel Plant Germany ke collaboration se establish hua. [Q198]\n• Rourkela Steel Plant West Germany ke collaboration se develop hua tha, Soviet collaboration se nahi. Maharashtra Elektrosmelt\nLimited ko 2011 mein SAIL ke saath merge kiya gaya. [Q199]\n• Bokaro Steel Plant erstwhile Soviet Union (USSR) ke collaboration se establish hua. [Q200]\n• Bokaro Steel Plant erstwhile Soviet Union (USSR) ke collaboration se establish hua tha; USA ke collaboration se nahi. [Q201]\n• Integrated steel-plant State mapping: Bhilai—Chhattisgarh; Bokaro—Jharkhand; Durgapur—West Bengal; Rourkela—Odisha.\n[Q202]\n• Muri aluminium/alumina industrial centre Jharkhand mein located hai, Chhattisgarh mein nahi. [Q203]\n• Jajpur (Odisha) ka integrated iron and steel plant Neelachal Ispat Nigam Limited se associated tha, Steel Authority of India se nahi;\nlater Tata-group associate ne ise acquire kiya. [Q204]\n• Indian Diamond Institute (IDI) Surat mein located hai. Institute gems aur jewellery manufacturing mein technical skills, quality,\ndesign aur global competitiveness improve karne par focus karta hai. [Q205]\n• Cement-industry centre mapping: Sikka (Gujarat)—1; Katni (Madhya Pradesh)—2; Churk (Uttar Pradesh)—3; Tirunelveli (Tamil\nNadu)—4. [Q206]\n• Industrial centre-industry association important hai; raw material, energy, labour, market aur transport jaise factors industrial\nlocation ko strongly influence karte hain. [Q207]\n• Aonla—fertilizer, Modinagar—rubber, Barabanki—poly fibre aur Kanpur—explosives important centre-industry pairs hain. [Q208]\n• Coimbatore—cotton textiles, Rourkela—iron & steel, Kapurthala—railway coach aur Barauni—oil refining important industrial pairs\nhain. [Q209]\n• Tuticorin—pearl fishing, Pune—automobiles, Marmagao—shipbuilding aur Pinjore—engineering goods important centre-industry\nassociations hain. [Q210]\n• Industrial-resource centre mapping: Singrauli (Madhya Pradesh)—coal; Kajarhat (Uttar Pradesh)—cement; Koyali (Gujarat)—oil;\nAnand (Gujarat)—milk. [Q211]","• Tronica City Ghaziabad district, Uttar Pradesh mein located hai; Noida mein nahi. [Q212]\n• National Automotive Board Ministry of Heavy Industries ke under aata hai, Ministry of Commerce & Industry ke under nahi; Coir\nBoard Ministry of MSME ke under hai. [Q213]\n\nEXAM TRAP — Steel Plants — Partner Country & Location\n▸ Steel-plant mapping: Bhilai—USSR/Chhattisgarh; Rourkela—West Germany/Odisha; Bokaro—USSR/Jharkhand;\nDurgapur—United Kingdom/West Bengal.\n[Q195, Q196, Q197, Q198, Q199, Q200, Q201, Q202]\n\n\n\n\n13. National Renewal Fund, Golden Handshake & Industrial Relations\n\n• National Renewal Fund (NRF) February 1992 mein worker-protection framework ke roop mein establish hua. VRS, technology\nupgradation aur sick-unit closure se affected workers ke retraining, rehabilitation aur compensation par focus tha. [Q214]\n• Technology upgradation ya sick-unit closure se affected workers ke interests protect karna, retraining aur rehabilitation provide\nkarna NRF ka key purpose tha. [Q215]\n• 1991 reform period mein surplus public-sector employees ke liye incentive-based Voluntary Retirement Scheme (VRS) ko promote\nkiya gaya; ise commonly 'Golden Handshake' kaha gaya. [Q216]\n• National Renewal Fund ka major objective labour retraining tha. [Q217]\n• National Renewal Fund ka objective industrial restructuring aur technological change se affected workers ko social-security\nprotection, retraining aur rehabilitation support dena tha. Fund February 1992 mein establish hua. [Q218]\n• Golden Handshake voluntary retirement (VRS) se related concept hai. [Q219]\n• Golden Handshake Scheme voluntary retirement se related hai. [Q220]\n• South Korean company POSCO ne Odisha mein Paradip ke near major steel-project investment propose kiya tha. [Q221]\n• India Asia ka first country tha jisne Export Processing Zone model adopt kiya; Asia ka first EPZ 1965 mein Kandla, Gujarat mein\nestablish hua. Objective export production ko internationally competitive environment provide karna tha. [Q222]\n• Industrial development ke major constraints mein low savings-investment, weak infrastructure aur low purchasing power shamil\nrahe hain; ye demand aur productive capacity dono ko limit kar sakte hain. [Q223]\n• Labour-intensive industries mein capital ke comparison mein labour input ka relative importance zyada hota hai. Hotels,\nrestaurants, hospitality aur agriculture jaise sectors labour-intensive examples ho sakte hain. [Q224]\n• Industrial relations ke main stakeholders workers/unions, management/employer organisations aur government hote hain;\nconsumers ko direct co-partner nahi maana jaata. [Q225]\n\nEXAM TRAP — National Renewal Fund vs Golden Handshake\n▸ National Renewal Fund worker retraining/rehabilitation aur restructuring support se related tha; Golden Handshake voluntary retirement\n(VRS) se related hai.\n[Q214, Q215, Q216, Q217, Q218, Q219, Q220]\n\n\n\n\n14. Sugar, Cement, Textiles, Aluminium, Petrochemicals & Industrial Location\n\n• 2023-24 (P) sugar production data mein Maharashtra leading State tha. [Q226]\n• Sugar industry ka early concentration Uttar Pradesh aur Bihar mein tha. 1903 mein Pratappur, Deoria (UP) mein early modern\nsugar mill establish hui; UP ka sugarcane yield Maharashtra/Karnataka jaise States se comparatively lower raha hai. [Q227]\n• Sugarcane area ke context mein Uttar Pradesh leading State hai; Agricultural Statistics at a Glance 2024 ke 2024-25 data mein\ntotal sugarcane area ka around 49.92% UP mein tha. [Q228]\n• Sugar decontrol par committee C. Rangarajan ki chairmanship mein constitute hui thi; us waqt woh Prime Minister's Economic\nAdvisory Council ke Chairman the. [Q229]\n• Katni, Madhya Pradesh cement industry ke liye known hai; paper-industry centre ke roop mein identify nahi kiya jaata. [Q230]\n• Cement plants generally limestone sources ke near locate hote hain. 2024-25 context mein industry ka large share Rajasthan,\nAndhra Pradesh, Telangana, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, Gujarat, Tamil Nadu, Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Odisha,\nMeghalaya aur West Bengal jaise States mein concentrated tha. [Q231]\n• Industrial-centre mapping: Titagarh—jute goods; Bengaluru—silk textiles; Ludhiana—woollen textiles; Bhadohi—woollen carpets.\n[Q232]\n• HINDALCO ka Renukoot plant Uttar Pradesh mein Birla Group se associated hai. Location ka major factor abundant power\navailability tha; surrounding power projects ki wajah se region ko 'energy capital' bhi kaha gaya. [Q233]\n• Madras Aluminium Company (MALCO) Mettur, Salem district (Tamil Nadu) mein located thi, Chennai mein nahi. Indian Aluminium\nCompany (INDAL) later Hindalco ka part bani. [Q234]\n• Gujarat petrochemical industry ka major State hai. Khambhat aur Ankleshwar important oil fields hain; feedstock availability ne\nAnkleshwar mein petrochemical complex ke development ko support kiya. [Q235]\n• Coastal Gujarat ke Porbandar, Dwarka, Bhavnagar, Vadodara, Jamnagar aur Surat jaise cities textiles, cement, fertilizers,\nchemicals aur petrochemicals ke important industrial centres hain. [Q236]","• Participation in management ka matlab workers ko enterprise ke policy/management decisions mein representation dena hai; trade-\nunion representatives ya elected workers ko management board mein place diya ja sakta hai. [Q237]\n• Ranchi, Jharkhand ki capital, Chota Nagpur Plateau par located hai. [Q238]\n• Dewas, Madhya Pradesh ek important industrial city hai aur currency-note printing se famous hai. [Q239]\n• Industry capital-intensive hai ya labour-intensive—ye mainly capital investment aur labour input ke relative proportion se determine\nhota hai. [Q240]\n\n\n15. Industrial History, Business Groups, MNCs & Automobile Headquarters\n\n• Industrial firsts: first machine-made paper 1870 Calcutta; early cotton-mill attempt 1818 Calcutta unsuccessful raha; successful\ncotton mill 1854 Bombay ke near establish hui; first cement factory 1904 Madras ke near establish hui. [Q241]\n• Early industrial chronology: Bombay cotton textile mill (1854) → Rishra jute mill (1855) → steel production ka development →\nIndian-owned sugar industry ka expansion. [Q242]\n• VSNL ke disinvestment ke baad company Tata Group ke control mein aayi. [Q243]\n• Samsung aur LG multinational companies hain. Hindustan Unilever Limited India-headquartered listed consumer-goods company\nhai aur global Unilever group ki Indian subsidiary hai. [Q244]\n• Automobile-HQ mapping mein Renault—France aur Volkswagen—Germany correct pairs hain; BMW—USA aur Daimler—Sweden\nincorrect pairs hain. BMW ka headquarters Munich, Germany mein hai. [Q245]\n\n\n16. Khadi, Textile Committees, RIICO, State Finance & Industrialists\n\n• All India Khadi and Village Industries Board 1953 mein First Five Year Plan ke dauran establish hua; 1957 se iska role statutory\nKhadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC) ne take over kiya. [Q246]\n• Khadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC) ka headquarters Mumbai mein hai. 1957 mein constituted statutory body hai aur\nMinistry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises ke under function karti hai. [Q247]\n• Tarapore Committee rupee ki capital-account convertibility par recommendations ke liye constituted hui thi; customer service ya\nindustrial sickness committee nahi thi. [Q248]\n• Handloom sector development ke liye 1995 mein Mira Seth ki chairmanship mein 12-member committee bani. Committee ne ₹500\ncrore ka National Handloom Fund establish karne ki recommendation ki. [Q249]\n• Textile-industry reforms ke liye Sathyam Committee July 1998 mein constitute hui; report August 1999 mein submit hui aur National\nTextile Policy 2000 par is committee ki recommendations ka influence tha. [Q250]\n• Unorganised/informal sector enterprises ko support karne ke liye Central Government ne September 2004 mein Arjun Sengupta ki\nleadership mein National Commission constitute kiya. [Q251]\n• Rajasthan State Industrial and Mineral Development Corporation (RSIMDC) 28 March 1969 ko Companies Act, 1956 ke under\nindustrial aur mineral development accelerate karne ke liye establish hua. [Q252]\n• RIICO ne industrial units/investment cooperation ke liye Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) ke saath MoU sign kiya tha.\n[Q253]\n• State Financial Corporations State-level institutions hain jo SMEs ko term loans, equity/debenture subscription, guarantees, bill\ndiscounting aur other financial assistance provide karte hain. [Q254]\n• Industry/brand-person mapping: Reliance—Mukesh Ambani; Airtel—Sunil Bharti Mittal; Nano—Ratan Tata; Wipro—Azim Premji.\nWipro ko R. Krishnamurthy se pair karna incorrect hai. [Q255]\n\n\n17. e-Biz, E-Commerce, Information Technology & Software\n\n• e-Biz portal 2013 se government-business services ke single-window platform ke roop mein develop hua. Objective online G2B\nservices access badhakar business environment improve karna tha. [Q256]\n• E-Commerce ka basic meaning internet ke through business transactions karna hai. [Q257]\n• E-commerce internet ke through goods/services ka exchange aur money/data transmission hai. Iske advantages mein global reach\naur relatively low transaction/operating cost shamil hain. [Q258]\n• M-Junction 2001 mein Tata Steel aur SAIL ke 50:50 joint venture ke roop mein establish hui. FY2020 context mein transaction\nvalue around 14.7 billion report ki gayi thi. [Q259]\n• India mein 1990s se information technology ka rapid development hua. Software/services base strong raha, lekin hardware base ko\nequally strong nahi maana ja sakta. [Q260]\n• Forbes January 2025 data mein TCS India's most valuable software company rahi. [Q261]\n\n\n18. Automobile, Pharmaceutical Sector & District Mineral Foundations\n\n• Automobile sector Indian economy ka key pillar hai. 2021-end context mein sector se around 5.3 crore direct aur indirect\nemployment linked bataya gaya; liberalisation aur policy support se capacity expansion bhi hua. [Q262]","• India vaccine production aur generic medicines mein major global supplier hai. Economic Survey 2022-23 context mein pharma\nproduction value ke basis par 14th aur volume ke basis par 3rd rank; generic medicines ke global volume supply mein around 20%\nshare bataya gaya. [Q263]\n• MMDR Act, 2015 amendment ke through mining-affected districts mein District Mineral Foundations (DMFs) establish karne ka\nprovision kiya gaya. [Q264]\n\n\n                              Exam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Industrial Sector Full Mind Map"];
